TeleOCR support in CrispEmbed
============================

CrispEmbed's original code remains under its MIT license. TeleOCR-specific
adaptations identified in source-file comments, and tools/teleocr_parse.py,
incorporate work under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The complete Apache
license is in models/licenses/apache-2.0/LICENSE. Retain this notice and that
license when redistributing these portions or a binary containing them.

Model weights license
---------------------
Qwen is licensed under the Qwen RESEARCH LICENSE AGREEMENT, Copyright (c) Alibaba Cloud. All Rights Reserved.
Built with Qwen.
TeleOCR's vision encoder derives from Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct (docs/teleocr-license.md);
the TeleOCR weights may be used for non-commercial purposes only. The agreement
text is in models/licenses/qwen-research/LICENSE. This applies to the model
weights, not to CrispEmbed's source code.

Inference architecture and reference
------------------------------------
XingChen-AGI / China Telecom: TeleOCR model and checkpoint.
https://huggingface.co/XingChen-AGI/TeleOCR
Revision: b3f6a0c084db72f971e19a779d2fd8a6bc9e3b8d

modeling_naviocr.py carries the following upstream attribution:
Copyright 2025 The Qwen Team and The HuggingFace Inc. team. All rights reserved.
It states that its code is based on EleutherAI's GPT-NeoX library and the
GPT-NeoX and OPT implementations in Transformers, with modifications for
architectural differences. That file is licensed under Apache-2.0.

Rust reference and document processing
--------------------------------------
teleocr-rs, by Rija Z. (@rzafiamy), Apache-2.0.
https://github.com/rzafiamy/teleocr-rs
Revision: 957cdbabe80e86d652c5fcc938ed7fbcf1eb2bbe

Reference files include crates/teleocr/src/image.rs, vision.rs, text.rs,
model.rs, pipeline.rs and otsl.rs. The Python document-parser adaptation in
tools/teleocr_parse.py derives from pipeline.rs and otsl.rs. This is a new
native ggml integration and a Python adapter for CrispEmbed's native binding;
it is not the upstream Rust/Candle implementation.
Related regression checks are in tests/test_teleocr_parse.py.

The original-module numerical diagnosis tools in
tools/teleocr_diagnostics/vision_layer17.py,
tools/teleocr_diagnostics/decoder_layer2.py and
tools/teleocr_diagnostics/_common.py, with tests/test_teleocr_ffn.cpp,
retain Apache-2.0 attribution to the licensed Qwen/Hugging Face model source.

Changes for CrispEmbed
----------------------
New GGUF schema and validation, native ggml tensor wiring, scoped preprocessing
and generation behavior, C ABI/CLI/orchestrator/binding integration, reference
capture and tests. The document parser is adapted to the native C ABI through
the existing Python binding. See docs/teleocr-license.md for the source audit.

The GGUF converter is newly authored MIT code which reads model data and does
not execute checkpoint Python. Converted model weights retain the publisher's
Apache-2.0 declaration; conversion does not relicense them as MIT.

No repository-wide permission is inferred for caipeng328/TeleOCR from its
model-card license. Its unlicensed document-client/post-processing Python
files are not included or directly translated in this integration.
